      "fit": 0.91
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Despite being outspent by his rival, the political trailblazer overcame a resource gap and, with a late-stage endorsement from the sitting president, achieved a landslide victory ending an era. This decisive voter-driven rejection of the old guard in the politically significant state saw the long-serving establishment figure become the first incumbent Texas Republican senator to lose renomination since 1970. The endorsed candidate now secures a place on the ballot for a high-stakes future challenge.",
